  - lib/review/src/graph.rs      (same pattern)

## `can_coerce_to` duplicates `satisfies` on Cardinality

can_coerce_to checks self.satisfies(target) then repeats the same
predicate. The intended distinction ("lossless injection") isn't
implemented. If coercions that alter cardinality but preserve
information are needed later (scalar→list by wrapping, optional→list
by empty/singleton), this needs explicit allowed-coercion rules,
not just set containment.

Files:
